{"id":"p1x8","name":"Sessionize click events","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["events","gap"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>A website logs every click as a pair <code>[user, ts]</code>, where <code>user</code> is a string and <code>ts</code> a timestamp in seconds (integer). The list <code>events</code> is <b>not sorted</b>, and a user can click twice in the same second.</p>\n<p>A <b>session</b> of a user is a group of consecutive clicks (in time order) where the time between two consecutive clicks is at most <code>gap</code> seconds. A click that comes strictly more than <code>gap</code> seconds after the previous click of the same user starts a new session.</p>\n<p>Return every session as <code>[user, start, end, clicks]</code>, where <code>start</code> and <code>end</code> are the first and last timestamps of the session and <code>clicks</code> the number of clicks. Sort the result by <code>user</code>, then <code>start</code>.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>events = [[\"ana\", 100], [\"bob\", 50], [\"ana\", 2000], [\"ana\", 60], [\"bob\", 1850]], gap = 1800</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[[\"ana\", 60, 100, 2], [\"ana\", 2000, 2000, 1], [\"bob\", 50, 1850, 2]]</pre>\n<p>For <code>\"ana\"</code>, the click at <code>2000</code> comes <code>1900</code> seconds after the click at <code>100</code>, which is more than <code>1800</code>: a new session starts.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.array.string events<br><b>[input]</b> integer gap<br><b>[output]</b> array.array</div>","starter":"def solution(events, gap):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":["ENTRÉE : clics en désordre. CLÉ : l'utilisateur. Regroupe les ts par user dans un dict, puis trie chaque liste.","Parcours les ts triés en gardant start, prev et n. Quand ts - prev > gap, ferme la session en cours et ouvre-en une nouvelle.","N'oublie pas d'ajouter la dernière session après la boucle."],"summary_fr":"Des clics [user, ts] dans le désordre. Pour chaque utilisateur, une nouvelle session commence quand il s'est passé PLUS de gap secondes depuis le clic précédent. Renvoie [user, début, fin, nombre de clics] trié par user puis début.","tags":["tri","dict","boucle","sessions"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"events":[["ana",100],["bob",50],["ana",2000],["ana",60],["bob",1850]],"gap":1800},"expected":{"value":[["ana",60,100,2],["ana",2000,2000,1],["bob",50,1850,2]]}},{"input":{"events":[["u",0],["u",0],["u",10]],"gap":10},"expected":{"value":[["u",0,10,3]]}}],"hidden_n":7,"hidden":"","solution":""}